      "text": "Montrose was founded in 1861 by George M. Wright, who named the town after his Pennsylvania hometown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/montrose_minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Montrose became an incorporated village in 1881, marking its official status as a community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/montrose_minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early growth sprang from a post office set up in Wright’s home in 1866 and the arrival of the railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/montrose_minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Hawkins Clinic, Hospital, and House, built in the early 1900s, now sits on the National Register of Historic Places.",
